BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty - Therapy Dog Prep/CGC (Lea Pfeiffer)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260923T001000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260923T010500Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260905T155804Z
UID:1790122200_Specialty-TherapyDogPrep/CGC@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Therapy Dog Prep and CGC\nWould you like to share your dog’s
  companionship with people in hospitals\, nursing homes\, schools\, or eve
 n in communities recovering from stressful situations or disasters? Therap
 y dogs provide comfort\, emotional support\, and affection in these settin
 gs.\nThe most important qualities of a therapy dog are temperament and sta
 bility. Is your dog friendly with both people and other dogs? Does your do
 g enjoy being petted and hugged by adults and children? How does your dog 
 respond to sudden loud noises or unexpected situations?\nIf your dog is ca
 lm\, gentle\, and enjoys interacting with others\, they may be an excellen
 t candidate for this therapy dog class.\nCanine Good Citizen\nThe CGC clas
 s is the first step to also becoming a Therapy Assistant Dog.  The 10 beh
 aviors that are learned in the CGC class will apply to the first 10 steps 
 in the Therapy test.  Therefore we combine the classes together so that w
 hatever your goals may be that you can accomplish that without having to t
 ake a separate class.\nThe AKC's Canine Good Citizen (CGC) program is reco
 gnized as the gold standard for dog behavior. Would you love for people to
  point at your dog and say\, I want my dog to act like that. That is what 
 we strive for in this class. We train for the 10 behaviors/commands that a
 re required for your dog to pass the Canine Good Citizen test.\nIf you wan
 t to know more about the CGC program\, click on this link\nhttp://www.akc.
 org/dog-owners/training/canine-good-citizen/what-is-canine-good-citizen/
END:VEVENT
